why:    a run's repo is git's common-dir parent, as runlog.py records it, and check and pending match on it, so a writer that recorded the working directory instead would scope runs differently from runlog.py wherever a symlink sits in the path (macOS's /var -> /private/var, a symlinked checkout). The frozen gate keeps the unresolved path under its own placeholder so this stays visible on any machine where the two differ.
